On Friday 04 December 2009, Agustin Lobo wrote:
> Is there a version of RKward for Mac OS (i.e. Leopard)?
> Plans for it? While the default GUI for Mac is good, RKward is better...

RKWard uses some X11-specifics, so I suppose it cannot be compiled natively for 
Mac OS. I think it should work with X11 on Mac just fine, but I'm pretty 
ignorant about this, and I don't even know, whether that would imply 
installing X11-versions of KDE, Qt and R as well.

Creating a native version for Mac OS should not be too hard, I believe, but 
obviously it would require someone with at least basic knowledge of Mac OS, 
and access to a Mac for testing. As you will have guessed, I don't have 
either. If anybody would like to give it a shot, I'd be happy to help as much 
as I can, but I just can't port it myself.

Regards
Thomas
